From: kaiwater <kaiwater@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 19:50:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7996: advertise beacon protection support

The mt7996 driver already implements the AP-side pieces that 802.11
beacon protection needs:

  - BIGTK (key index 6/7) installation into the second hardware key slot
    with IEEE80211_KEY_FLAG_GENERATE_MMIE (mt7996_set_hw_key())
  - BIP cipher mapping and firmware key TLV setup
    (mt7996_mcu_sta_key_tlv())
  - a beacon remove/re-add cycle to arm the firmware as soon as the
    BIGTK is installed (mt7996_set_hw_key())

What is missing is only the capability advertisement.  Without
NL80211_EXT_FEATURE_BEACON_PROTECTION hostapd treats the driver as
unsupported, hostapd_wpa_auth_conf() silently clears beacon_prot and the
BIGTK is never negotiated, so no MMIE is ever appended to the beacons.

Advertise the feature so the existing implementation becomes reachable.
This is the same thing iwlwifi (AP + client) and ath12k already do
upstream; there is no hardware limitation for mt7996/mt7992 here, only
the missing bit.

Signed-off-by: kaiwater <kaiwater@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 mt7996/init.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

--- a/mt7996/init.c
+++ b/mt7996/init.c
@@ -528,6 +528,7 @@
 	wiphy_ext_feature_set(wiphy, NL80211_EXT_FEATURE_ACK_SIGNAL_SUPPORT);
 	wiphy_ext_feature_set(wiphy, NL80211_EXT_FEATURE_CAN_REPLACE_PTK0);
 	wiphy_ext_feature_set(wiphy, NL80211_EXT_FEATURE_MU_MIMO_AIR_SNIFFER);
+	wiphy_ext_feature_set(wiphy, NL80211_EXT_FEATURE_BEACON_PROTECTION);
 	wiphy_ext_feature_set(wiphy, NL80211_EXT_FEATURE_SET_SCAN_DWELL);
 	wiphy_ext_feature_set(wiphy, NL80211_EXT_FEATURE_PUNCT);
 	wiphy_ext_feature_set(wiphy, NL80211_EXT_FEATURE_SCS);
